<title>LATVIA: NVEKS BROKERAGE SAYS Q1 PROFIT 20,000 LATS.</title>
<headline>NVEKS BROKERAGE SAYS Q1 PROFIT 20,000 LATS.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvian Inveks brokerage, which has been bought by Estonia's Hoiupank , on Tuesday said its first quarter profit came to 20,000 lats.</p>
<p>&quot;Our first qaurter profit this year is 20,000 lats,&quot; Yevgeny Bogdanov, executive manager of Inveks, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;Inveks had losses of some 3,700 lats in 1995 and we came break-even with the profit we made in 1996,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Inveks declined to disclose the price of the 76 percent stake paid by the Hoiupank.</p>
<p>The brokerage, founded in 1995, has share capital of 45,240 lats.</p>
<p>-- Martinsh Gravitis, Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
